# rust
/target/
# Every run cargo-mutants leaves behind, whatever it is called. It rotates
# mutants.out to mutants.out.old itself, and a third run kept
# under a name chosen by hand — so the glob is what makes the next invented name safe.
/mutants.out*/

# herdr: the released bdi herdr/fetch.sh installs.
/bin/

# the plugin's bun workspace
node_modules/
/plugin/dist/

# nix
result
result-*
.direnv/

# beads: a local tracker's workspace is not part of this repository. This entry
# is tracked rather than left to .git/info/exclude so it travels with the
# clone — `cargo publish` uploads the git-tracked tree, and that is exactly
# the machine with a populated .beads/.
/.beads/

# Machine-local: credentials, the dev shell selection, and the notes that go
# with them. Never leave the machine.
.env.local
.envrc.local
CLAUDE.local.md
.beads-credential-key

# Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db

# bd 1.3.0 leaves this behind after a read.
/.beads.gate.lock

# A linked worktree is a checkout of this repository, not a source file.
.claude/worktrees/

# python: the frame tooling under tools/capture/ is run rather than imported,
# but running it writes a cache beside it either way.
__pycache__/
